{"step_index":533,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:12:10Z","input_tokens":3044,"cache_read_tokens":74564,"output_tokens":1948,"thinking":"Examining the data structures in `explainer.js`, different event types reveal pertinent information. \"AUG_ASSIGN\" events provide details on variable modifications, while \"CONDITION\" events expose the logic behind conditional branching. Specifically, the \"c >= ans\" condition in \"CONDITION\" events suggests a comparison that can be framed as a true/false evaluation, especially during even iterations or the initial condition check.\n\n\nFocus is now on formulating prediction questions for different event types. For \"ASSIGN\" events targeting \"ans,\" the question will be \"What will ans become?\" For \"ASSIGN\" events where \"c\" is reset to 0, the question will be \"Why does c reset to 0?\" or \"What value is assigned to c to reset the negative sum?\" Question generation should also incorporate current variable values for clarity and context.\n\n\nQuestion phrasing is finalized for different event types. Conditionals will trigger \"True or False?\" questions, incorporating variable values. Assignment operations will prompt \"What will [variable] become?\" questions. Teaching substeps trigger interactive questions before execution.\n\n\nThe next step involves verifying the quiz mode functionality. Specifically, the agent needs to ensure the quiz card hides and renders correctly when the quiz mode is toggled on and off. Auto Play behavior will also be tested, confirming it pauses when a quiz question is encountered. Finally, score tracking will be checked to confirm correct values are maintained.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js","EndLine":1452,"StartLine":1400,"toolAction":"Checking end of explainer.js","toolSummary":"Check end of explainer.js"}}]}
